# --- QA screenshot churn -------------------------------------------------
# Verification screenshots are regenerated on every build and were never meant
# to be versioned. 1,516 of them had accumulated (390 MB) before this rule.
# They are QA evidence for a single build, not artefacts of the repo.
# Exception (do NOT ignore): 02_dashboards/pricing/_build/aim_truck_catalogue_2026-09-18/dmax_render/**
#   REVIEW_DMAX_RENDER.html embeds qa_accuracy_sheet.png as page content, and the
#   render tree is a designed visual set, not throwaway QA.
**/_qa/**
**/_qa_*/**
**/_qa*/*.png
**/_qa*/*.jpg
**/_qa*/*.jpeg
**/_qa*/*.webp
**/_qa*/*.gif
**/_gpt_review/**
_tmp_*.png
_tmp_*.jpg
_qa*.png
_qa*.jpg
# NOTE: no `!dmax_render/**` negation here on purpose. A broad negation would
# override the __pycache__/ and *.log rules below for that whole tree, which is
# how 132 .pyc and .log files got swept back into the index. The D-Max _qa sheets
# and _assets are already tracked and stay tracked; the pattern rules simply do
# not apply to them retroactively.

# --- D-Max render intermediates ---
# Only the per-frame PNG renders live here (346 MB). The _raw/*.json camera and
# silhouette measurements are INPUTS that measure_silhouette_mismatch.py reads
# (HERO_REPORT = _raw/cam_hero.json), so the folder itself must stay tracked —
# ignore the images only, never the folder.
02_dashboards/pricing/_build/aim_truck_catalogue_2026-09-18/dmax_render/_raw/*.png
02_dashboards/pricing/_build/aim_truck_catalogue_2026-09-18/dmax_render/_raw/*.jpg
02_dashboards/pricing/_build/aim_truck_catalogue_2026-09-18/dmax_render/_raw/*.jpeg

# --- 02_dashboards/Data deploy mirror ------------------------------------
# A real folder (not a junction) holding copies of derived data for published
# HTML, plus ingest leftovers. The root .gitignore excludes the canonical
# copies under 01_data/, so the same files were being tracked twice here:
# pricing_pn_enquiry_active.csv (98 MB), pricing_list_pn.csv (58 MB),
# sales_fact.csv (45 MB) and 900 other files, 414 MB in total. Canonical
# source is 01_data/, never this path.
02_dashboards/Data/

# --- Python bytecode that escaped the global __pycache__/ rule ---
# The D-Max render tree was reaching the index through a broad negation in the
# QA block above; these are compiled caches and run logs, never source.
**/__pycache__/**
**/*.pyc
02_dashboards/pricing/_build/aim_truck_catalogue_2026-09-18/dmax_render/**/*.log

